meta {
  name: Bare root
  type: http
  seq: 5
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/
  body: none
  auth: none
}

settings {
  encodeUrl: true
  followRedirects: false
}

tests {
  test("answers the explanatory page rather than nothing", function () {
    expect(res.getStatus()).to.equal(404);
    expect(res.body).to.contain("Snip turns long web addresses");
  });
}

docs {
  Somebody typing the short domain with no code after it. There is nothing to
  redirect them to, so they get the page that explains what the service is and
  links across to sign-up.

  The headline still reads "This link doesn't exist", which is not quite what
  happened here — an open question rather than a settled one. The alternative
  is redirecting the root across to the dashboard, which is a product decision
  nothing in the spec has made yet.
}
